TECHO5 Spot builds on the work of other open-source projects.

TECHO5, https://github.com/HuskerMinion/techo5 (MIT)
  The echod daemon, the Linux image tooling, the rootfs slot design and the kernel build recipe.

TECHO5 Dot (MIT)
  The 512 MB image layout and the installer and backup pattern.

EchoLocal, https://github.com/ygelfand/echolocal
  Copyright (c) 2026 Yuri Gelfand, MIT License.
  The original Echo Dot 2 daemon that echod was ported from.

amonet, kaeru and the Echo TWRP trees, https://github.com/R0rt1z2
  The unlock and bootloader payload this project depends on (not redistributed).

amazon-oss, https://github.com/amazon-oss
  The LineageOS 18.1 rook device tree and the MT8163 4.9 kernel, cited in docs/.

docs/dumps/rook_defconfig-lineage-18.1 is arch/arm64/configs/rook_defconfig from
github.com/amazon-oss/android_kernel_amazon_mt8163, branch lineage-18.1 (GPL-2.0), copied as a
reference; docs/dumps/rook-vs-cronos-defconfig.diff compares it with cronos_defconfig from the same tree.
